ntdll: process exit returns to boot with the full Windows status
(docs/design/wine-unix.md, section 8, "Process exit (M3)"; abi.md v5,
"Process exit").

Why: Wine ends the host process with the status cut to an exit code
(get_unix_exit_code, L89-94: a nonzero status with a zero low byte becomes
1, and _exit keeps only the low 8 bits). The Unix side is one instance in
the JS host, which needs the full status, and boot's promise must resolve
rather than end the runtime.

- exit_process (L1520-1524) and abort_process (L1485-1488) first call
  tw_process_exit(status) (native/wine/src/boot.c), before
  get_unix_exit_code. It records the status and longjmps to boot, which
  resets env.depth to 0 and returns the status. The longjmp unwinds the
  translated frames on the wasm stack as a wasm exception.
- exit_process is NtTerminateProcess's end for the current process once
  RtlExitUserProcess's first NtTerminateProcess(0, status) set
  process_exiting (dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c L965-985), and exit_thread's
  for the last thread (L1501); abort_process is NtTerminateProcess's for a
  process that never made that first call (process.c L982).

Line numbers are wine-11.0's dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c unless another file
is named.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -86,6 +86,12 @@
 
 static LONG nb_threads = 1;
 
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+/* Tempwind's process exit (wine-unix.md, section 8): records the full
+ * Windows status and longjmps to boot, which returns it (boot.c). */
+extern void DECLSPEC_NORETURN tw_process_exit( int status );
+#endif
+
 static inline int get_unix_exit_code( NTSTATUS status )
 {
     /* prevent a nonzero exit code to end up truncated to zero in unix */
@@ -1484,6 +1490,9 @@
  */
 void abort_process( int status )
 {
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+    tw_process_exit( status );  /* the full status, before get_unix_exit_code cuts it */
+#endif
     _exit( get_unix_exit_code( status ));
 }
 
@@ -1519,6 +1528,9 @@
  */
 void exit_process( int status )
 {
+#ifdef __wasm64__
+    tw_process_exit( status );  /* the full status, before get_unix_exit_code cuts it */
+#endif
     pthread_sigmask( SIG_BLOCK, &server_block_set, NULL );
     process_exit_wrapper( get_unix_exit_code( status ));
 }
